# Platypus-Bear {1}{G/U}, 2/3 defender: "When this creature enters, mill two cards" and "As long as there is a Lesson card in your
# graveyard, this creature can attack as though it didn't have defender" (CR 701.17, 702.3b, 609.4). The mill puts a Firebending Lesson and a Plains
# into Bot1's graveyard (one Lesson is enough), so on turn 3 the Bear attacks (Bot2 20 -> 18). The condition is about the Bear alone: Bot1's Sylvan Caryatid, a
# defender too, is refused.

[Bot1 Deck]
Platypus-Bear
Sylvan Caryatid
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Forest
Plains
Firebending Lesson
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

